		"cbf801cc-94cd-4bc7-9416-209664ee665e": {
			"id": "cbf801cc-94cd-4bc7-9416-209664ee665e",
			"shortId": "I2.1",
			"type": "impl",
			"content": "在 sanitizeToolUseId 中增加：若 ID 以 call_ 开头（OpenAI 原生 ID），直接返回原值，跳过字符替换",
			"status": "done",
			"parentId": "d66da17a-39a6-4c95-baf0-49dfb816c3eb",
			"childrenIds": [],
			"codeBindings": [
				{
					"commitHash": "fa92dcebb980f7c605c7866315e004f4802e821e",
					"commitMessage": "[intent:I2.1] fix: skip sanitization for OpenAI-native call_ IDs to prevent tool-result mismatch\n\nOpenAI generates call IDs with the \"call_\" prefix that may contain base64\ncharacters (+, /) in __thought__ suffixes. Sanitizing these IDs replaces\nthose characters with underscores, but OpenAI internally tracks the original\nID — causing \"tool_result does not match any tool_use\" errors.\n\nFix: return call_ prefixed IDs unchanged in sanitizeToolUseId(). The\nsanitization logic is still needed for Gemini/OpenRouter IDs (e.g.\nfunctions.read_file:0) which contain dots and colons that violate the\n^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$ pattern required by the OpenAI API.",
					"files": [
						".roo/cache/search/index.json",
						".roo/intent-tree.json",
						"src/core/prompts/tools/native-tools/consult_expert.ts",
						"src/utils/__tests__/tool-id.spec.ts",
						"src/utils/tool-id.ts"
					],
					"diffSummary": "5 file(s), +132 -129",
					"timestamp": "2026-02-20T02:19:50.249Z"
				}
			],
			"createdBy": {
				"taskId": "019c78d7-674c-727e-b1cc-fdf53d866618",
				"timestamp": "2026-02-20T02:18:59.405Z",
